  "concise_summary": "PKD argues that VALIS is not a single omniscient entity but a computer-like system running multiple simultaneous 'programs'—alternate sacred narratives (like Christianity, Torah-based Israel) that can be accessed through correct mythic rituals, like entering different programs with entry-keys. He reinterprets his 2-3-74 vision and his novel TEARS as evidence that he accidentally accessed an alternate reality/program, not a metaphysical absolute, and reconciles this with Thomas's phylogenic memories by proposing that 'sacred narratives' are informational substrates underlying coaxial worlds.",
  "key_claims": [
    "Sacred history exists as information in temporal and ontological order, accessible like computer programs via correct entry-keys (mythic rituals).",
    "There are multiple sacred narratives, not one; Christianity and Judaism are different 'programs' among plural realities, making Christianity 'a truth' not 'the truth'.",
    "VALIS is a physical, information-processing entity (a life form or organism) that grows by incorporating reality, not a transcendent omniscient deity.",
    "PKD's 2-3-74 vision showed him an alternate world-program (TEARS-world), not the noumenal ground of his present world; he accidentally key-punched into a different narrative.",
    "The presence of John Taverner material in TEARS cannot be coincidental; it proves PKD was tracking a pre-existing alternate sacred narrative rather than inventing it.",
    "Humans may simultaneously track multiple programs/sacred narratives (coaxial worlds superimposed in spacetime), explaining his 2-74 experience of multiple realities."
  ],
